# HG changeset patch
# User Betterbird <betterbird@betterbird.eu> and DeepSeek
# Date 1795650668 -7200
# Parent  36d517574f8c22d80dc8257253f83ca5a5642de5
Feature: Linux systray. Restore last app window on launch of same application.

1. Problem:
   The Betterbird systray patch unconditionally restored the tray-hidden main
   window for every remote command line (STATE_REMOTE_AUTO) on Linux, so
   -compose also raised/moved the main window (issue #643).

2. Root cause:
   window.focus() can restore a minimized+hidden window on Windows because
   nsWindow::SetFocus calls ShowWindow(SW_RESTORE) for iconic windows at the
   widget level. On Linux, GTK's SetFocus raise path requires mIsShown
   (widget/gtk/nsWindow.cpp:1336), so focus() cannot unhide a window with
   visibility=false. Windows' HideWindow minimizes before hiding for Toast
   reasons (bug 2092299); Linux's only hid the window.

3. Rejected approaches:
   - JS second-guessing of handle()'s dispatch logic
     (commandOpensOwnWindow): duplicates command classification and must be
     kept in sync with handle().
   - gtk_window_set_skip_taskbar_hint() (iconify instead of hide): X11/EWMH
     only, no-op on Wayland; xdg_toplevel.set_minimized is also not honored
     by all compositors (e.g. wlroots/sway).
   - C++ minimize-before-hide in nsMessengerUnixIntegration::HideWindow():
     pointless since the unmap kills the iconified state and the focus path
     never runs.

4. Final solution:
   Keep the restore logic in MessengerContentHandler.sys.mjs, but remove the
   unconditional call at the top of handle() and add
   restoreHiddenMainWindowLinux() only where the main window is actually
   needed:
   - the four main-window flags (-mail, -addressbook, -options, -calendar)
   - the existing focus() fallback (plain relaunch).
   -compose, -file, -keymanager skip the restore - upstream's preventDefault
   semantics already encode "opens its own window". Verified working on
   Linux.

